NNAAMMEE
       ipcmk - make various IPC resources

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       iippccmmkk [options]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       iippccmmkk allows you to create System V inter-process communication (IPC)
       objects: shared memory segments, message queues, and semaphore arrays.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       Resources can be specified with these options:

       --MM, ----sshhmmeemm _s_i_z_e
           Create a shared memory segment of _s_i_z_e bytes. The _s_i_z_e argument may
           be followed by the multiplicative suffixes KiB (=1024), MiB
           (=1024*1024), and so on for GiB, etc. (the "iB" is optional, e.g.,
           "K" has the same meaning as "KiB") or the suffixes KB (=1000), MB
           (=1000*1000), and so on for GB, etc.

       --QQ, ----qquueeuuee
           Create a message queue.

       --SS, ----sseemmaapphhoorree _n_u_m_b_e_r
           Create a semaphore array with _n_u_m_b_e_r of elements.

       Other options are:

       --pp, ----mmooddee _m_o_d_e
           Access permissions for the resource. Default is 0644.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

